{
	quest.0048F33DB9D8BA07.quest_subtitle: "Found in Jungle Pyramids"
	quest.0127885DC2B5B237.quest_subtitle: "Found in Nether Fortresses"
	quest.032970B17A7186E1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shulker Boxes&r have received some buffs in this pack, so they aren't completely overshadowed by backpacks."
		""
		"They work like bundles now, where you can click items on them to put the items into the Shulker Box. You can then scroll over the Shulker Box to select an item inside of it to extract from."
		""
		"Similar to backpacks, they show a + icon if items can be inserted into them. The + is yellow when no same item is in the Shulker Box and green when there is."
	]
	quest.08AAEE51833A0222.quest_desc: [
		"Before you're able to go to the End, you need to collect special eyes that you will need to open the portal."
		""
		"Worst case, you only &9need a max of 12 of the eyes&r listed here. This all depends on how many eyes are already inside of the end portal frames that you find."
	]
	quest.08AAEE51833A0222.title: "Prerequisite"
	quest.0904D1F646BFD460.quest_subtitle: "Found in Desert Pyramids"
	quest.0F34B1FABE39F438.quest_subtitle: "Found in Basion Treasure Chests"
	quest.14C73547918AC836.quest_subtitle: "Kill a Witch"
	quest.150CA0E67B46F908.quest_desc: ["Dude, stop. It's already dead..."]
	quest.150CA0E67B46F908.title: "&zDragon Extinction&r"
	quest.2588D8A4CADFD477.quest_subtitle: "Found in Buried Treasure"
	quest.288D8D1A7FE38879.quest_desc: [
		"See this strange looking forest? Silently watched over by the &eFallen Stars&r of the End sky, grow &eVivid Nihilium&r and &ePream Trees&r. These last have yellow and blastproof wood, just like Endstone! They also yield &ePream Berries&r from their foliage, which also heal you when eaten."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Now let's look at the other side of the mirror. Below the &6Dreaming Den&r is the &eUnderisland&r, which could be considered a sub-biome. The roof is covered in &eOblivion&r, a strange void corrupted moss that can be used as a repair material for anything, and &eOblivines&r. You can latch to them not to fall, and they grow &eOblifruits&r, which have a chance not to be consumed on use!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Lastly, scattered both above and below the biome are glowing &eCrystal Spikes&r. They are mainly useful for crafting decorative blocks, but the ones below the islands have a chance to be &eVoided&r, which can be crafted into tools that mine faster the more experience you have, acting as an upgrade to gold."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In this new place spawn two new mobs, the &eCrystie&r and the &eBehemoth&r."
		""
		"&eCrysties&r are little crystal fairies, with an explosive filiation with &eEnd Crystals&r. Would you dare to hit one, it would then attempt to dive straight into you to explode in a sparkly bang, or simply when it dies."
		""
		"&eBehemoths&r are lazy giants sleeping anywhere on the ground of the &6Dreaming Den&r. Be careful though, as getting too close will wake them up, and they're quite grumpy! They are immune to knockback and ranged attacks, but drop powerful physical enhancing meat when defeated."
	]
	quest.28FB92E97612915B.quest_desc: ["The Ender Dragon now drops meat items that you can use to make various dragon based food."]
	quest.28FB92E97612915B.title: "Cook... the Dragon?"
	quest.29755FE008C28594.quest_desc: ["Strange wormholes found throughout the End that can teleport you to another part of the dimension."]
	quest.2B8DB5675D534207.quest_subtitle: "Kill an Elder Guardian"
	quest.2C98C5DDA98FD70C.quest_subtitle: "Found in Pillager Outposts"
	quest.2CCB20A497104EA6.quest_desc: [
		"Throughout the End, you will find some odd spices that you will be able to use to make some peculiar dishes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Ethereal Saffron"
		"{image:endersdelight:item/ethereal_saffron width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Bizarre plant that seems to be able to regenerate when cut, resulting in two."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Amberveils"
		"{image:endersdelight:item/amberveils width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"Unusual fungi that are able to \"corrupt\" other fungi into itself."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Chorusflame"
		"{image:endersdelight:item/chorusflame width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"A spicy flower that can grow into more when planted on End Stone."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Voidpepper"
		"{image:endersdelight:item/voidpepper_sprout width:50 height:50 align:center}"
		""
		"A bizarre fruit that can spread to other End Stone blocks when planted. It bears fruit after a while, which can then be harvested by either breaking it or shearing it."
		"It loses the ability to spread after a while. This can be reset by breaking it and placing it back."
	]
	quest.2CCB20A497104EA6.title: "Strange Spices"
	quest.2CEBC36598CC89F2.quest_subtitle: "Found in Mineshafts"
	quest.30D78033FCCFB36A.quest_desc: ["There are several biomes and structures that you can find in the End! Try exploring them all."]
	quest.30D78033FCCFB36A.title: "Biomes \\& Structures"
	quest.3293D6A063383BCD.quest_subtitle: "Found in Igloos"
	quest.34C2FF061DBE8013.quest_subtitle: "Buy it from a master Cleric"
	quest.3D016A926E0EB70E.quest_desc: [
		"After you have collected the eyes, you will now need to find a Stronghold. Then you'll be ready to enter the End."
		""
		"Make sure you're well prepared for the End. You most importantly will need some form of traversal option, as not only are the islands bigger, but can also be above each other. Consider getting some Relics like the &bWarp Drive&r or &bPhantom Boots&r, &ba plane&r from Immersive Aircraft, &ba grappling hook&r or even &ba Pokémon capable of flight&r."
	]
	quest.3D016A926E0EB70E.title: "Find a Stronghold"
	quest.3D13C9D094E63030.quest_desc: ["You're now able to live in the End thanks to the &6End Respawn Anchor&r. It works like the Nether version, where you can charge it with either &bEnder Pearls&r or &bEyes of Ender&r and everytime you die, you instead respawn next to the Anchor, using one charge."]
	quest.3EAAD1829E6E57E0.quest_desc: ["The &6Void Barrens&r is a desolated mountainous biome, full of &bBlackstone&r, &bObsidian&r and &bSmooth Basalt&r, where everything is either dead or not born yet."]
	quest.41D1366551168847.quest_desc: ["Slay the dragon and free the End dimension from its grasps!"]
	quest.41D1366551168847.title: "Kill the Dragon"
	quest.433E63073948E6C3.quest_desc: [
		"&eShulker Box&r can now be enchanted with some pretty neat &eenchantments&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lVacuum&r"
		"Comes in two levels. Whenever the player picks up an item, it tries to insert the item into the shulker box, as long as the slot has space for it."
		""
		"The first level ignores empty slots and won't let the item in, even when there's empty space. The second level adds items to the shulker box, while allowing them to enter empty spaces."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lVoid&r"
		"Like the first level of Vacuum, but items are voided if they exceed the stack limit."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lRefill&r"
		"When the block you're placing runs out in your inventory, the shulker box will try to refill, if it has the same block."
	]
	quest.433E63073948E6C3.title: "Shulker Enchantments"
	quest.44623DDD83BC0DCA.quest_desc: [
		"Wished you could dye your &eShulker Boxes&r like the &ebackpacks&r? Thanks to the &6Shulker Dyeing Station&r that's now possible!"
		""
		"Inside of the station you can mix and match dyes to get a color, similar to how you'd dye leather armor or backpacks."
		""
		"Not only that, but you can give the top and the bottom halves different colors!"
	]
	quest.45375AE6AA0A34AC.quest_desc: ["The remains of what used to be a dragon. Now only good for plant fertilizer"]
	quest.457A78F92BCB72A1.quest_desc: [
		"Worried about creepers blowing up your shulker boxes? No more!"
		""
		"Applying a &6Hardened Shulker Template&r and &eObsidian&r to a &eShulker Box&r in a &eSmithing Table&r will harden it, making it completely resistant to explosion, even in item form!"
		""
		"These upgrades can be found in ancient cities and end cities."
		""
		"&8<turb a=0.2>Did you know that nether stars are immune to explosions?</turb>&r"
	]
	quest.4759BDDEADFF2E42.quest_desc: ["The &6Crystal Peaks&r biome is a gloomy, mountainous biome full of &bBlackstone&r, &bSmooth Basalt&r, &bObsidian&r and &bCrying Obsidian&r with blobs of &bAmethyst&r blocks. Despite being prominent in the biome, Amethyst blocks drop only one eighth of the time. "]
	quest.57673244C1DC1FFA.quest_subtitle: "Crafted using an Undead Soul"
	quest.5B12795B38EBB0C8.quest_desc: ["The classic End biome. Full of &bChorus&r and sometimes &eEnd Cities&r."]
	quest.5B3209A05A23883D.quest_subtitle: "Kill a Skeleton Horse"
	quest.5DEABFB7624DD781.quest_desc: ["An &6End Ship&r from an &eEnd Castle&r. Even though it's small, it still contains some good loot in it."]
	quest.60DD78F2CF59797F.quest_desc: ["Welcome to the End of Minecraft! Now defeat the Ender Dragon &8or just dip and go straight to the outer islands&r."]
	quest.60DD78F2CF59797F.title: "Enter the End"
	quest.6234B792075167B7.quest_desc: [
		"Legends have it that centuries ago, when more Dragons ruled over the End, one of them went mad and ravaged the starry landscapes below, destroying all life and letting islands scarred with acid waste and cracks."
		""
		"That is, of course, only legends and nightmares. Or is it? Dreams have proven to come true."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Although, the environment adapted, growing plants made of obsidian and pulling nutrients from the everlasting acid. Rocks formed from melted endstone, bringing and concentrating all kinds of minerals from within the islands. Formed a biome reminiscent of both the deepest oceanic floors and the lushiest jungles: Meet the &6Acidburnt Abysses&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Below thrives a rather peculiar lifeform, here in the &6Choral Riff&r."
		""
		"Choral learnt to live off the void's echoes and whispers, gaining all sorts of musical properties. It can be used to craft &eSubwoofers&r to push entities when powered, and &eChoral Arrows&r to unleash the power of music right in your foe's face!"
	]
	quest.662D43BA7208BEEB.quest_subtitle: "Kill a Wither"
	quest.6836306E4B4A3313.quest_subtitle: "Kill an Evoker"
	quest.6AAE5D9954E1EF9B.quest_subtitle: "Crafted using aquatic items"
	quest.6B716018F00CDAE2.quest_desc: [
		"Scared of accidentally throwing your shulker box into lava, while trashing items? Then get a &6Plated Shulker Upgrade&r!"
		""
		"Applying it with an &eNetherite Ingot&r in a &eSmithing Table&r will make the Shulker Box completely resistant to fire and lava, like netherite!"
		""
		"These can be found in treasure bastions."
	]
	quest.7107B3ED5ECCD3C5.quest_subtitle: "Crafted using a Witch Pupil"
	quest.714F989FEA8AE9B8.quest_desc: ["The classic vanilla &6End City&r. Containing a bunch of &bShulkers&r and sometimes even the famous &bElytra&r."]
	quest.72BBE9A926BBBFF4.quest_desc: ["The &6Shadowlands&r is a dark and barren biome made out of &bDead Coral&r. To add to this, the barren wasteland is full of dragon bones, ribs, limbs, and sometimes, entire &eDragon Skeletons&r can be found floating around. "]
	quest.7837C80AD5C4D7DF.quest_desc: ["A GIANT structure, resembling and &eEnd City&r floating in the air. It is filled with loot that are guarded by &bTrial Spawners&r."]
	quest.7FABB6BF34901DFF.quest_desc: [
		"Huh, strange. Seems like the method of obtaining this eye has been magically hidden."
		"Maybe it has something to do with experience based on its looks?"
	]
	quest.7FABB6BF34901DFF.quest_subtitle: "&kThe description of the eye is the link to Never Gonna Give You Up."
